From 39cafa17abadb96618a924c5c638a050f4623327 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x399 <x399@lab>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:53:49 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] nvk/nvrm: let the GPU use memory the application owns

VK_EXT_external_memory_host, implemented with resman's OS descriptors:
the driver pins the pages and maps them into the GPU's address space, so
a window's bitmap can be written by the GPU instead of by the CPU.

The wait for a submission also no longer sleeps through poll(), which
costs a millisecond a time however short a timeout is asked for: it
spins first and then sleeps in short steps, which took an empty
submission from 1.08 ms to 13 us.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
